openmediavault-qnap (8.0.6) stable; urgency=low

  * One-file install: the driver packages now ship inside the plugin, so
    it can be uploaded on System > Plugins without a command line.
  * Drivers page: a Set up drivers button installs the kernel headers and
    the bundled drivers, starts them (retrying with skip_hw_check on models
    that need it), loads them at boot and turns fan control on. It replaces
    Install kernel headers, and also updates the drivers after a plugin
    update.
  * Plain-language pages for people new to Linux: fan speeds in percent,
    no jargon, rare options under Advanced, friendly sensor names on the
    Status page and dashboard grid, and plain light states on Disks.

 -- Nader Eloshaiker <1904325+nader-eloshaiker@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:05:10 +1100

openmediavault-qnap (8.0.5) stable; urgency=low

  * Kernel headers: the Drivers page shows whether headers for the running
    kernel are installed, and Install kernel headers adds them plus the
    metapackage that brings headers for future kernels
    (proxmox-headers-X.Y on the Proxmox kernel, linux-headers-<flavour> on
    Debian), so DKMS keeps rebuilding the drivers after kernel updates.

